\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{A curved square changes the first-order square}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{The uncoupled counting operator of \ref{fdip-00OL} combines a
degree-raising difference with its degree-lowering adjoint.
Replacing each ordinary difference by a coefficient transport
puts the two paths around a square into its square. Which
pairing makes backward transport the adjoint, and which
identities survive when those paths disagree?}
